p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 335)</h2>
<p><b>Notes from busy people — offline, before, or after the review.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Comments written in the browser with no connection now survive the tab and deliver themselves the next time the page opens — nothing is lost to a train tunnel.</li>
<li>Comments that arrived while you were away are badged in the notes sidebar ("N arrived while you were away") so a busy list can't swallow them.</li>
<li>Joining a review with notes or marks you made outside it — on a plane, before the invite — now offers to share them: attributed to you, filed to the right clips, never shared without asking. Content for clips the room doesn't have yet waits and files in when the clip appears.</li>
<li>If a review's picture has expired, the web page now says so and keeps taking comments instead of dead-ending — they still reach your next session.</li>
<li>The pointer tool now shows a dashed selection around a clicked mark, and Delete removes it — in the app, matching the web. Guests can select and delete their own marks; the host any.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
